| `shell.script_suffixes` | list of strings | `[".sh", ".bash"]` | a non-empty list, each a `.` and at least one more character, with no whitespace or `/` | `scripts/shell_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `shell.script_suffixes` row | Sets which file names make a file a shell script that the lint and format targets judge, beside any file whose shebang `shell.shebang_shells` names; a name that also ends in `.jinja` is a template's source and is never judged. Removing a suffix hides those files from every shell gate. A malformed list is exit 14. Absent, the targets write `[using default] shell.script_suffixes = [".sh", ".bash"]` to stderr. | test files: `shell.test_suffixes` | always |
